What is the output of the following inheritance copy constructor program?
```java
class BaseShape {
    int colorCode;
    BaseShape(int c) { this.colorCode = c; }
    BaseShape(BaseShape other) { this.colorCode = other.colorCode; }
}
class CircleShape extends BaseShape {
    int radius;
    CircleShape(int c, int r) { super(c); this.radius = r; }
    CircleShape(CircleShape other) {
        super(other);
        this.radius = other.radius;
    }
}
public class SubCopyMain {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        CircleShape c1 = new CircleShape(12, 5);
        CircleShape c2 = new CircleShape(c1);
        System.out.println(c2.colorCode + "," + c2.radius);
    }
}
```

What is the output of the following array list copy constructor program?
```java
import java.util.ArrayList;
import java.util.List;
class TeamRoster {
    List<String> names;
    TeamRoster(List<String> n) { this.names = n; }
    TeamRoster(TeamRoster other) {
        this.names = new ArrayList<>(other.names); // collection copy
    }
}
public class RosterMain {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        List<String> original = new ArrayList<>();
        original.add("Sam");
        TeamRoster r1 = new TeamRoster(original);
        TeamRoster r2 = new TeamRoster(r1);
        r2.names.add("Mia");
        System.out.println(r1.names.size() + ":" + r2.names.size());
    }
}
```

